<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>JRuby series</th>
      {%- for base_image in base_images %}
        <th>{{ base_image }}</th>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for row in rows %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.major_minor }}</td>
        {%- for release in row.releases %}
          <td>{{ release or "-" }}</td>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

To use a JRuby version, specify it in your `Gemfile`. For example:

```ruby
# Gemfile
ruby '{{ example.ruby_compat }}', engine: 'jruby', engine_version: '{{ example.version }}'
```

Then, with that JRuby version installed locally, update your `Gemfile.lock` by running:

```term
$ bundle update --ruby
```
